@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It writes its positional objects as raw text: each object is converted with ``str()`` and the results are joined by ``sep`` (a space by default), followed by ``end`` (a newline by default)::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep=", ")
+
+:meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` does not pretty-print containers, wrap or crop text, process console markup, or replace emoji codes. Text is written literally.
+
+It does apply highlighting, which is on by default. Pass ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the Console's own setting. It also accepts a ``style`` argument, which is applied in the same way as for print.
+
+
